{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeReducedCost","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeReducedCost","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeCompletion","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.support_subset_of_bound_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.support_subset_of_bound_tight","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L169-L180","doc":"**Equality concentrates the coefficients on the maximiser.** If `m₀` is the only monomial of\nthe support with `|t| = M` (all others strictly below), equality in the cost bound forces\n`c_m = 0` for every `m ≠ m₀` in the support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.bound_tight_of_aligned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.bound_tight_of_aligned","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L158-L167","doc":"**Sufficiency.** If every weight on the support has `|t_m| = M` and every product\n`c_m · t_m` is non-negative, the cost bound is an equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_eq_of_bound_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_eq_of_bound_tight","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L132-L156","doc":"**Necessity.** If `|Σ c_m t_m| = M · Σ |c_m|` and `|t_m| ≤ M` on the support, then\n`|t_m| = M` at every `m` in the support with `c_m ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.linearFunctional_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.linearFunctional_one","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L106-L112","doc":"On the identity element the functional is the weight of the empty word,\nand the cost is `1`; so when `t [] = M` the bound is attained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_linearFunctional_nf_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_linearFunctional_nf_le","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L95-L104","doc":"The bound in terms of a reduced cost: whichever normal form is used, the\nfunctional evaluated on it is bounded by `M` times the reduced cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_scaled_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_scaled_le","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L87-L93","doc":"The cost bound after a non-negative scale `s`. For the mass,\n`s = [2]ⁿ q^(−2w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_linearFunctional_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.abs_linearFunctional_le","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**The cost bound.** A coefficient-linear functional whose weights on the\nsupport are bounded by `M` is bounded by `M` times the cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.linearFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.linearFunctional","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L71-L74","doc":"A functional linear in the coefficients, with weight `t m` on monomial `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost.nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost.nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L65-L69","doc":"The reduced cost is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost.unique","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**The reduced cost is single-valued.** Two normal forms of one element in\nthe completed system are equal (`heckeCompleted_normalForm_unique`), so they\nhave the same cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ReducedCost.IsReducedCost","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeReducedCost.lean#L49-L53","doc":"`c` is the Hecke cost of a normal form of `f` in the completed system. ","signatureChunk":0}]}